  <h1>Digital Millennium Copyright Act (DMCA) Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Effective Date: October 2026 | Version 3.5</em></p>

  <p>
    <strong>YouTube to MP4</strong> (<code>ytubeconvert.site</code>, "the Service", "the Platform", "we", "us", or "our") respects the intellectual property rights of creators, filmmakers, musical artists, visual authors, and media publishers. It is our strict policy to respond expeditiously to legitimate notices of alleged copyright infringement in full compliance with the provisions of Title II of the Digital Millennium Copyright Act (codified at 17 U.S.C. &sect; 512, "DMCA") and relevant international copyright treaties.
  </p>
  <p>
    This page sets forth our operational copyright policy, explains our technological role as an automated transient transmission conduit, provides the statutory contact information for our Designated Copyright Agent, and details the precise requirements for submitting valid takedown notices and counter-notifications.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Technical Architecture &amp; Transitory Digital Network Communications Safe Harbor</h2>
  <p>
    To assist copyright proprietors in understanding our technological operations, please be advised of the following foundational architectural facts:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No Permanent Content Hosting:</strong> YouTube to MP4 does not host, store, broadcast, or maintain a persistent repository of copyrighted video or audio streams on our servers. Our servers function strictly as an automated, on-demand format multiplexing and transcode proxy.</li>
    <li><strong>User-Initiated Ephemeral Processing:</strong> Every conversion task executed on our platform is initiated exclusively at the voluntary, self-directed request of an individual user who supplies a publicly accessible third-party URL.</li>
    <li><strong>15-Minute Automatic Purge:</strong> Any intermediate media files generated during stream multiplexing exist solely in temporary cache directories for the minimal duration required to transmit the stream to the user's browser, and are permanently wiped by our automated cleanup daemon within 15 minutes.</li>
    <li><strong>Transitory Communications Safe Harbor:</strong> Our platform qualifies for the statutory limitations on liability established under 17 U.S.C. &sect; 512(a) (Transitory Digital Network Communications) and 17 U.S.C. &sect; 512(c) (Information Residing on Systems or Networks at Direction of Users).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Requirements for Submitting a Legally Valid DMCA Takedown Notice</h2>
  <p>
    If you are a copyright owner or an agent authorized to act on behalf of an owner of an exclusive right that is allegedly infringed, and you believe that our utility is being utilized to access your copyrighted material without authorization, you must submit a written notification pursuant to 17 U.S.C. &sect; 512(c)(3).
  </p>
  <p>
    To ensure prompt processing by our legal compliance department, your notice must include substantially the following statutory elements:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Physical or Electronic Signature:</strong> A physical or digital signature of a person authorized to act on behalf of the owner of an exclusive copyright right that is allegedly infringed.</li>
    <li><strong>Identification of the Copyrighted Work:</strong> Precise identification of the copyrighted work claimed to have been infringed, or, if multiple works at a single online site are covered by a single notification, a representative list of such works (including title, registration numbers if applicable, or original publisher URLs).</li>
    <li><strong>Identification of the Target YouTube URLs:</strong> Specific identification of the material that is claimed to be infringing or to be the subject of infringing activity, including the exact YouTube URL(s) (e.g., <code>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=...</code>) that you request our service block from conversion. General inquiries or requests to "block all videos by a creator" without specific URL links cannot be processed by our automated filtering systems.</li>
    <li><strong>Complainant Contact Information:</strong> Information reasonably sufficient to permit our compliance department to contact you, including your full legal name, company or organization, physical mailing address, telephone number, and an active email address.</li>
    <li><strong>Good-Faith Belief Statement:</strong> A formal statement: <em>"I have a good-faith belief that use of the material in the manner complained of is not authorized by the copyright owner, its agent, or the law (such as fair use)."</em></li>
    <li><strong>Accuracy &amp; Perjury Statement:</strong> A formal statement: <em>"The information in this notification is accurate, and under penalty of perjury, I am authorized to act on behalf of the owner of an exclusive right that is allegedly infringed."</em></li>
  </ol>

