    <p><strong>Response Timeline:</strong> We review and act upon compliant statutory notifications within 24 to 48 business hours of receipt.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>4. Technical Enforcement: URL Blacklisting Protocol</h2>
  <p>
    Because our platform does not permanently store user-submitted videos, traditional "file removal" is technically not applicable. Instead, upon receipt of a valid, fully compliant DMCA notification, our compliance engineers execute the following preventative blocking protocol:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>API Gateway Domain &amp; Video Blacklisting:</strong> The reported YouTube video IDs are immediately entered into our API gateway's global blocklist database.</li>
    <li><strong>Automated Rejection:</strong> Any subsequent user attempt to input, query, parse, or convert the blacklisted URL triggers an immediate HTTP 403 Forbidden error response: <em>"This video has been permanently blocked from conversion pursuant to a validated DMCA copyright takedown request."</em></li>
    <li><strong>Channel-Level Blocking:</strong> In instances where a copyright holder owns an entire channel catalog and demonstrates sustained infringement, our engineering team can apply wildcard filtering to disallow all video URLs associated with the specific YouTube Channel ID.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Statutory Counter-Notification Procedure (17 U.S.C. &sect; 512(g))</h2>
  <p>
    If you are a content creator whose video link was blocked on our platform and you believe in good faith that the restriction was instituted as a result of mistake, misidentification, or that you hold legitimate legal rights (such as an open Creative Commons CC-BY license or fair use authorization), you may submit a written Counter-Notification pursuant to 17 U.S.C. &sect; 512(g)(3).
  </p>
  <p>
    Your Counter-Notification must contain the following statutory components:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Your physical or electronic signature.</li>
    <li>Identification of the specific video URL that was blocked by our service.</li>
    <li>A statement under penalty of perjury: <em>"I have a good faith belief that the material was blocked or disabled as a result of mistake or misidentification of the material to be removed or disabled."</em></li>
    <li>Your full legal name, physical address, and telephone number.</li>
    <li>A statement that you consent to the jurisdiction of the Federal District Court for the judicial district in which your address is located (or if outside the United States, any judicial district in which the service provider may be found), and that you will accept service of process from the person who provided the original takedown notice.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Upon receipt of a valid Counter-Notification, we will forward a copy to the original complaining party. If the copyright owner does not file a legal court action seeking an injunction within 10 to 14 business days, we may restore conversion availability for the contested URL.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Mandatory Warning: Penalties for Perjury &amp; Misrepresentation (17 U.S.C. &sect; 512(f))</h2>
  <p>
    Please note that under Section 512(f) of the Digital Millennium Copyright Act, any person who knowingly materially misrepresents that material or activity is infringing, or that material or activity was removed or disabled by mistake or misidentification, <strong>shall be liable for any damages</strong> (including costs and attorneys' fees) incurred by the alleged infringer, by any copyright owner or copyright owner's authorized licensee, or by a service provider who is injured by such misrepresentation.
  </p>
  <p>
    Furthermore, under the landmark precedent established in <em>Lenz v. Universal Music Corp.</em> (799 F.3d 1126), copyright owners are legally required to consider whether the contested use constitutes <strong>statutory Fair Use</strong> before issuing a formal DMCA takedown notification.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Policy on Repeat Infringers</h2>
  <p>
    In accordance with 17 U.S.C. &sect; 512(i)(1)(A), YouTube to MP4 maintains an active, strict policy for terminating access to the Service for users who are determined to be repeat infringers. While our system does not require registered accounts, our firewall actively monitors IP address clusters and API keys. Any automated script, IP subnet, or API consumer that repeatedly attempts to process known blacklisted URLs or violate our Terms of Service will face permanent IP blocking and firewall termination without notice.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Questions and Contact Information</h2>
  <p>
    For all copyright compliance inquiries or clarification regarding our takedown protocol, please email <a href="mailto:ytubeconvert@gmail.com?subject=DMCA%20Policy%20Inquiry">ytubeconvert@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>
